{
  "configuration_id": "config_027",
  "reason": "Evidence: Only one experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) has been completed, yielding ~48.5% accuracy. This establishes a baseline for the RNA modality but leaves the central question unanswered: does adding the image modality improve performance? Uncertainty: We have no information about whether image features carry complementary signal, whether they help or hurt, or which image encoder is effective. This experiment (config_027: multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, None, concat) directly tests the effect of adding a strong image encoder (ImageNet-pretrained ViT-L) to the exact same RNA setup as config_001, keeping profile setting (singleprofile) and RNA encoder (pca_n2000) constant. The only change is the addition of the image modality with a simple concat fusion, making this a clean single-factor comparison. Why this is the best next experiment: It directly addresses the most important design decision for a multimodal study—whether the image modality adds value at all—while minimizing confounds. The result will either validate the multimodal direction (justifying further investment in image encoders, fusion, and aggregation) or show that images do not help (redirecting effort toward RNA encoder or profile choices). This is the highest-information experiment available given the current sparse evidence."
}

